    "body": "## Problem\n\n`do_search()` repeats a search when the pattern is followed by `;`, as in `/foo/;/bar`. It skips both the `;` and the following search direction, but only decrements `patlen` once, so `patlen` is one byte too long for the repeated search.\n\nThat extra byte is the pattern's NUL terminator, which is copied into the search message buffer. `cmdline_search_stat()` writes the count at the *end* of the buffer, i.e. behind that NUL, so the count of a repeated search is lost. Observed `search_count` payloads for `/foo/;/foo`:\n\n```\n{ \"/foo            [2/2]\" }   -- first search\n{ \"/foo\" }                    -- \";\" repeat: count is gone\n```\n\nWith ui2 this is worse than a missing count: `ui2/messages.lua` extracts the count with `:match()` and concatenates the result, so a message without one raises `attempt to concatenate a nil value`.\n\n## Solution\n\nSubtract the two skipped characters from `patlen`, so a repeated search keeps a NUL-free message, reports its count like any other search, and gives ui2 something to parse.\n\nThe new `messages2` test fails on `master`: row 14 shows the ui2 error instead of `/foo           W [1/2]`.\n\n<details><summary>Actual screen before the fix</summary>\n\n```\n|{10:^foo}                                                  |\n|bar                                                  |\n|{10:foo}                                                  |\n|...\n|*{1:<<<}{9:tring \"vim/_core/editor\"]:411>}                    |\n```\n\n</details>\n\nAlso verified the counts and directions for `/foo/;?foo`, `/foo/;/bar/;?foo`, `/foo/;/foo/+1`, `/foo/s-1;?foo` and a four-deep `/bar/;/bar/;/bar/;/bar` chain (each step emits a bracketed count, and the counts follow the cursor):\n\n```\n\"/foo            [2/2]\", \"?foo            [1/2]\"\n\"/foo            [2/2]\", \"/bar            [2/2]\", \"?foo            [2/2]\"\n\"/foo            [2/2]\", \"/foo/+1          W [1/2]\"\n\"/foo/s-1            [1/2]\", \"?foo            [1/2]\"\n\"/bar            [1/2]\", \"/bar            [2/2]\", \"/bar          W [1/2]\", \"/bar          W [2/2]\"\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- `stylua --check`, `clang-format --dry-run --Werror`\n- `TEST_FILE=test/functional/ui/messages2_spec.lua`: 34 tests pass (incl. the new one)\n- `TEST_FILE=test/functional/ui/messages_spec.lua`: 86 tests pass\n- `make oldtest TEST_FILE=test_search.vim`: 82 tests; `test_search_stat.vim`: 12 tests\n- functional `ui` and `editor` groups pass\n\ncloses #41929\n\nAI-assisted\n",
